sequenceDiagram
    autonumber
    participant W1 as Worker W1 (processing M)
    participant Sched as CompileScheduler
    participant W2 as Worker W2 (pool)
    participant Live as symbol_tables (live DashMap)

    Note over W1,Live: Target state (option b, in-call-stack). M's in-progress cluster state lives only on W1's process_cluster stack frame. No module_sexps / suspend_states. The only cross-thread fact is the scheduler's monotonic terminal-readiness signal.

    W1->>W1: process_cluster(shared, sexps_M, M) — expand, build, Pass-0 peel, check_forms over stack-local staging_M

    alt check_forms returns Ok
        W1->>Live: commit staging_M to Live[M] (atomic drain under write guard)
        W1->>Sched: notify_typecheck_done(M)
        Note over W1: Cluster complete. No map touched.
    else check_forms returns Err(Gap(N)) — M needs module N
        W1->>W1: drop staging_M (atomic discard, Live[M] unchanged, nothing parked)
        W1->>Sched: ensure_registered(N) — parse N to a fresh packet carrying sexps_N, register_module(N), wake pool
        W1->>Sched: block_for_typecheck(M, N, sym)
        Note over Sched: detect_cycle_locked FIRST (Decision 30). Mutual import M to N to M is rejected before any wait. No cycle here, so add W1 as waiter on N.
        W1->>Sched: park in wait_for_typecheck (W1 yields, pool slot not held busy)

        W2->>Sched: take_priority_work_blocking — claims packet for N
        W2->>W2: process_cluster(shared, sexps_N, N) returns Ok
        W2->>Live: commit staging_N to Live[N] (atomic)
        W2->>Sched: notify_typecheck_done(N)

        Sched-->>W1: sweep waiter — clear M.blocked_on, requeue M's packet (sexps_M ride the packet)
        Note over W1: Resume is retry-from-top, not resume-at-index. No saved Pass-2 index, so Defect-B semantics hold by construction.
        W1->>W1: re-run process_cluster(shared, sexps_M, M) from the top — Pass-0 peel of (import N) now resolves (N in Live), check_forms Ok
        W1->>Live: commit staging_M to Live[M]
        W1->>Sched: notify_typecheck_done(M)
    end

    Note over W1,Live: Soundness — in-progress cluster state is stack-local (no sharing, no race). Cross-thread signalling is monotonic-terminal-only (publish-once, observe-many). The resumer reads only committed Live[N]. This is the substrate-removal that closes the S60 to S62 heisenbug class.
